    LLM: 'Game: Derda. Execute deal and bid phase, enforce trick obligations, then score points and words toward 500.',
    Player: 'Choose the safer trump contract for this deal based on your high cards and likely sequence bonuses.',
    objective: "Be first to achieve cumulative score of 500 points across multiple deals. Points scored for cards taken in tricks and bonuses ('words').",
    gameplay: "1. First dealer chosen by drawing cards (higher card in trump order)\n2. Deal 6 cards to each player, turn up 13th card for suggested trump\n3. Bidding round 1: Non-dealer can 'play' suggested trump or 'pass'\n4. If non-dealer passes, dealer can 'play', 'pass', or ask 'how many times?'\n5. If both pass round 1, round 2 allows choosing different trump suit\n6. Commercial offers can be made to throw in hand for points/deal advantage\n7. Once trumps chosen, deal 3 more cards each\n8. Player with 7 of trumps may exchange it for turn-up card\n9. Non-dealer leads to first trick\n10. Must follow suit if able; must play trump if cannot follow (if have trump)\n11. Highest trump wins if trumps played; otherwise highest of led suit\n12. Winner leads to next trick",
